  "summary": "The Alameda County Board of Supervisors voted 3-2 to approve a one-year, $2.4 million extension of its Flock Safety contract covering ALPRs, drones, and data systems for the Sheriff's Office through June 2027. Opponents cited a recent SB 34 violation in which out-of-state entities accessed county camera data, and criticized liability caps in the contract; the Sheriff said offending deputies were removed from Flock access and a competitive bidding process is underway.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Alameda County Board of Supervisors approved a one-year $2.4 million contract extension for Flock Safety surveillance technologies with the Sheriff's Office in a 3-2 vote Tuesday",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "As recently as June, Alameda County camera data has been accessed by out-of-state entities, a violation of Senate Bill 34",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "The contract with the county stipulates that Flock Safety is liable for such breaches of personal identifiable information, but sets a maximum cap of liability as the total amount of money the county has paid within the last 12 months.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
